Modifications in this distribution (DoubaoPlot, a derivative work of EditaPlot)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DoubaoPlot is a derivative work of EditaPlot, built on the upstream project at
https://github.com/hang-jin/editaplot and redistributed under the same Apache
License, Version 2.0. The foundation and the original concept are hang-jin's. All
plotting logic, Origin automation routes, verification gates, gallery assets, and
scientific palettes are the work of the upstream EditaPlot contributors and are
used unchanged. The name DoubaoPlot applies to this derivative version only.

Changes made in this distribution, per Apache-2.0 section 4(b):

  1. Skill installation targets the 豆包工作 (Doubao Work) skill directory in
     addition to the upstream Codex directory, resolved by environment variable
     with autodetection and a fallback to the upstream behaviour.
  2. User-facing documentation and prompts are rewritten for 豆包工作 users.
     Technical identifiers, error codes, and sandbox-detection logic are
     unchanged.
  3. An interactive chart selector is added ahead of the existing workflow, so a
     user picks a chart visually instead of describing it in prose. It only
     assembles a request; it does not alter how anything is drawn.

No upstream plotting behaviour, data contract, or verification gate is modified
by these changes. This distribution is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or
supported by the upstream EditaPlot author.

Additional modifications (DoubaoPlot, 2026-09-05):
  4. skill/doubaoplot/scripts/bootstrap_editaplot.py detects Doubao's Windows
     LOCALAPPDATA workspace/.user_skills directory and explains the bootstrap
     entry point when runtime discovery fails.
  5. skill/doubaoplot/scripts/editaplot.py and editaplot_core.py add template-aware
     palette discovery and actionable mapping-role errors. The shared palette
     mode lookup and incompatible-palette message in
     runtime/src/origin_sciplot/scientific_workflow.py are updated without changing
     rendering behaviour or accepted palette modes.
  6. skill/doubaoplot/SKILL.md and references/semantic-understanding.md document
     Skill-only installation, exact mapping roles, palette filtering, and PNG
     presentation instead of attempting to foreground Origin. Regression coverage
     is added in tests/test_doubao_friction.py; the runtime manifest is rebuilt.

Additional modifications (DoubaoPlot, 2026-09-06):
  7. README.md and README.en.md are rewritten as DoubaoPlot's own documents. They
     describe this derivative directly for a first-time reader instead of carrying the
     upstream README with a note prepended, and they no longer refer readers to
     upstream-voiced documents inside this repository. Upstream attribution is kept and
     expanded into a dedicated section that names hang-jin and EditaPlot, states that
     the plotting capability is upstream's, retains the aggregate Star badge and Star
     trend chart, and asks readers to star the upstream repository. The 17 uncovered
     chart types are inlined. Upstream's coverage table, gallery images, palette image,
     permission scope, privacy statements, and scientific boundaries are retained.
  8. The optional WeChat tip section is removed from both READMEs, because the payment
     code belongs to the upstream author and this derivative does not solicit or handle
     payments on their behalf. The asset file assets/support/wechat-tip.png is kept
     tracked and unchanged. tests/test_public_release_gate.py replaces
     test_public_readmes_end_with_optional_support_section with
     test_public_readmes_credit_upstream_and_drop_the_tip_section, which asserts the tip
     section is absent from both READMEs and that both credit the upstream repository.
  9. skill/doubaoplot/scripts/bootstrap_editaplot.py accepts the DoubaoPlot Skill name in
     its install-time identity check. That check previously recognized only the upstream
     name, so every DoubaoPlot installation was rejected; the upstream name is still
     accepted so existing installations upgrade in place. A failed identity check is now
     reported as such instead of as a write-permission failure.
 10. skill/doubaoplot/selector/selector.py serves the selector page from its existing
     loopback HTTP server and no longer launches a system browser unless --open is given,
     so the host's own browser opens the page. SKILL.md and the user-facing documents are
     updated to match. Regression coverage is added in tests/test_doubao_friction.py.
     Neither change alters plotting behaviour, data contracts, or verification gates.
 11. The Skill source directory is renamed from skill/editaplot to skill/doubaoplot, so the
     repository layout matches the Skill name this derivative declares and installs. File
     names inside that directory are unchanged. The launcher, the repository-root probe,
     tools, tests, the release policy, the asset provenance manifest, and the documentation
     are updated to the new path, and both directory names are still accepted so an existing
     clone or installation keeps working.
